# Commits listed here are skipped by `git blame` when the repo (or the
# blamer's local config) points `blame.ignoreRevsFile` at this file:
#   git config blame.ignoreRevsFile .git-blame-ignore-revs
# One hash per line -- a trailing description on the same line makes git
# treat "<hash> <message>" as a single (unresolvable) revision spec and
# `git blame` fails outright: `fatal: invalid object name: <hash> <message>`.
# Only large, purely mechanical reformats belong here -- never a commit
# that changes behavior. dev/master are squash-merged, so a feature-branch
# SHA never lands there -- only the squash SHA from a PR containing
# NOTHING but reformatting may be listed; a squash that mixes formatting
# with anything else can't be, since ignoring it would hide the
# authorship of everything else in the same commit too.
